      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T06:28:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "annaherrera@ and mogenson@, can you recommends some standard reset/restart reasons by MCU?",
      "parentUuid": "78aea502_5b49d483",
      "revId": "f2419157a88ad27171b5d47a43c036bfceec3f57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "690ebbb8_0e91336e",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/IBluetoothSocketCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1999105
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T13:54:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only reason the MCU would restart it\u0027s offload stack is if there was an offload stack crash, a BT controller crash, or a MCU crash. In the passthrough mode, all of these would also result in a BTHAL and Android BT stack crash, so this onRestarted method would not be called. I don\u0027t have any suggestions for vendor specific status codes for our MCU.",
      "parentUuid": "8a30752d_b01d1466",
      "revId": "f2419157a88ad27171b5d47a43c036bfceec3f57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a50f573_4456832c",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/IBluetoothSocketCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T15:13:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this callback be removed then ?\nEven in non pass-through mode it might be indicated to restart the BTHAL / stack to reset the state after a MCU crash.",
      "parentUuid": "690ebbb8_0e91336e",
      "revId": "f2419157a88ad27171b5d47a43c036bfceec3f57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d32d3038_10b810af",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/IBluetoothSocketCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T17:42:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Depending on the offload architecture, an offload domain crash may not cause or require an Android BT stack crash. For example, in a sideband design, if an offload domain crash occurs, \bwe may only need to release the related BT offload socket, while in a passthrough design, we may need to force an Android BT stack crash. So, I think it is better to keep this callback to clean up all BT offload sockets when it is called.",
      "parentUuid": "1a50f573_4456832c",
      "revId": "f2419157a88ad27171b5d47a43c036bfceec3f57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4cc94a65_c4563efc",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/IBluetoothSocketCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-19T18:44:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Restarting all the BT services would be safer in ensuring that the state is properly reset I think. Doing this also enforces a common behavior for passthrough and sideband modes: the stack should not have to be aware of the difference.",
      "parentUuid": "d32d3038_10b810af",
      "revId": "f2419157a88ad27171b5d47a43c036bfceec3f57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
